=======================================================================
VENDORED CODE — internal/edwards25519, internal/edwards25519/field
=======================================================================

Derived from the Go standard library's crypto/internal/edwards25519 and
from filippo.io/edwards25519. The non-field vendored baseline is
filippo.io/edwards25519 v1.0.0; internal/edwards25519/field is synchronized
to filippo.io/edwards25519 v1.2.0, except for the modifications and
Narya-authored additions listed below. The source tags are:

    https://github.com/FiloSottile/edwards25519/tree/v1.0.0
    https://github.com/FiloSottile/edwards25519/tree/v1.2.0

The v1.2.0 field sync covers fe.go, fe_generic.go, fe_amd64.go,
fe_amd64.s, fe_amd64_noasm.go, and fe_extra.go, plus the upstream arithmetic,
alias, and wide-input tests in fe_test.go, fe_alias_test.go, and
fe_extra_test.go. On arm64, the v1.2.0 generic implementation replaces the
older Go standard-library carry-propagation assembly shim.

    Copyright (c) 2009 The Go Authors. All rights reserved.

BSD-3-Clause. The upstream LICENSE files are preserved verbatim in
internal/edwards25519/LICENSE and internal/edwards25519/field/LICENSE.

MODIFICATIONS. Narya has changed files in this tree relative to upstream:

  * internal/edwards25519/field/fe.go — relative to
    filippo.io/edwards25519 v1.2.0, the square-root-ratio computation retains
    Narya's derivation following BoringSSL (see below). The public behavior is
    unchanged, while this form saves two squarings and three multiplications.
  * internal/edwards25519/scalarmult.go — the leading-zero skip in
    VarTimeDoubleScalarBaseMult was rewritten. Upstream's loop iterates a
    local variable but returns the unmodified bound, so the skip is inert
    and 256 doublings always run; Narya's form actually advances the index.
    The computed result is unchanged. Narya also factors the common DSM loop
    and adds VarTimeDoubleScalarBaseMultTable for a previously prepared
    width-5 public-key table.
  * internal/edwards25519/tables.go — PubkeyNAFTable and its constructor were
    added for the prepared width-5 DSM path.
  * internal/edwards25519/extra.go — MultiScalarMult initializes its receiver
    to the identity before accumulating. This fixes a latent use of an
    uninitialized zero Point as an accumulator.
  * import paths were rewritten to the Narya module path throughout.

Standalone Narya-authored files inside this tree — including comb.go,
smallorder.go, equal_affine.go, field/sqrt_ratio_test.go, and their first-party
tests — carry Apache-2.0 headers. Modified upstream files retain their
BSD-3-Clause headers, including the Narya changes enumerated above. The
vendored v1.2.0 field arithmetic and upstream alias tests also remain
BSD-3-Clause.


